#THIS IS FILE IMPINIT, WHAT A C PROGRAM WITH A main OF ITS OWN CALLS TO START THE IMP72 RUNTIME: imp_init(argc, argv) KEEPS THE COMMAND LINE FOR THE IMP ROUTINES TO ASK FOR WITH CCALL: impargc(0) AND impargvp(0) FOR THE ARRAY.  IT IS A MEMBER OF ITS OWN, WITHOUT main AND WITHOUT THE MAIN PROGRAM, SO THAT A C PROGRAM THAT CALLS IT LINKS NEITHER (LIB/IMPMAIN.IML IS THE main THAT CALLS IT, LIB/IMPRUN.IML IS imp_run).  THE C CALLER GIVES ARGC AND ARGV BY VALUE; AN IMP ROUTINE TAKES ITS ARGUMENTS BY REFERENCE, SO THE VALUES ARE THE ADDRESSES IT IS GIVEN: LOC(ARGC) IS ARGC (THE LOW 32 BITS OF IT: THE REST OF THE REGISTER IS NOT DEFINED) AND LOC(ARGV) IS ARGV #
IMPACV,IMPAVV ARE COMMON;
SUBR impargc(Z) IS IMPACV;
SUBR impargvp(Z) IS IMPAVV;
SUBR imp_init(ARGC,ARGV) IS (
 IMPACV:=LOC(ARGC) AND 4294967295;
 IMPAVV:=LOC(ARGV) AND SCMASK(0);        # (A 32 BIT POINTER THAT COMES AS A PARAMETER IS SIGN EXTENDED: THE STACK IS ABOVE 2 GB) #
 IMPBINMODE(0);                           # (ON WINDOWS THE STANDARD FILES ARE MADE BINARY, SO THAT A PROGRAM WRITES THE BYTES IT MEANS) #
 0)
%%
